\\mathcal{O})\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_S)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\QCoh(S_\\tau, \\mathcal{O})\n$$", "MATHSEG_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}\\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "}\\mathcal{P}\n\\Leftrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}^a\\text{", "MATHSEG_0005": "}\\mathcal{P}\\text{", "MATHSEG_0006": "}\\mathcal{O}\\text{", "MATHSEG_0007": "}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\tau \\in \\{Zariski, \\linebreak[0] \\etale, \\linebreak[0]\nsmooth, \\linebreak[0] syntomic, \\linebreak[0] fppf\\}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0004": "$r$", "MATH_0005": "$r$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}^a$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{P}=$", "MATH_0009": "$\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_S) \\to \\QCoh(S_\\tau, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\tau$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-global}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-site-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{proposition-equivalence-quasi-coherent}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-equivalence-quasi-coherent-properties}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f3f5870c7a381f35e5d51262c9fad5aff31e6525e69c1761177aff3b3bfa55d9", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:61bd1f2c8e96f9bc9eba05e3e8e39e58c17434d5847c3dfe9b90f3a293637721", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ee68e43f8754cde7cb2e6caadb340f3dbe3a650ea68fce527aca5e5289920cf6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be one of the properties of modules<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>The list is:\nfree, finite free, generated by global sections,\ngenerated by <MATH_0004> global sections, generated by finitely many global sections,\nhaving a global presentation, having a global finite presentation,\nlocally free, finite locally free, locally generated by sections,\nlocally generated by <MATH_0005> sections, finite type, of finite presentation,\ncoherent, or flat.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001> defined in\nModules on Sites, Definitions <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\nThe equivalences of categories\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\ndefined by the rule <MATH_0006> seen in\nProposition <REF_0004>\nhave the property\n<MATHSEG_0003> has <MATHSEG_0004> has <MATHSEG_0005> as an <MATHSEG_0006>-module<MATHSEG_0007>\nexcept (possibly) when <MATH_0007> is ``locally free'' or ``coherent''.\nIf <MATH_0008>``coherent'' the equivalence\nholds for <MATH_0009>\nwhen <MATH_0010> is locally Noetherian and <MATH_0011> is Zariski or <ACCENT_0001>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f39dc87c03509df92a6e4fddf386a46724ebe0638d9215ca1acc736d5e0d4b66", "unit_id": "tag:05VG:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03DR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^a$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-global}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-local-final-object}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-descends}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-finite-presentation-descends}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-locally-generated-by-r-sections-descends}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-flat-descends}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-finite-locally-free-descends}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{coherent-lemma-coherent-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ecee0519eb310192435742db3e737ac91e97b661dde0c2b7a423ecf4f7e15ae5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:839895d6a456a0a957b14e6a9f789352745ece5f0daf1d9f664a509d37395f61", "source_text": "This is immediate for the global properties, i.e., those defined in\nModules on Sites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nFor the local properties we can use\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>\nto translate ``<MATH_0001> has <MATH_0002>'' into a property\non the members of a covering of <MATH_0003>. Hence the result follows from\nLemmas <REF_0003>,\n<REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>,\n<REF_0006>, and\n<REF_0007>.\nBeing coherent for a quasi-coherent module is the same as being\nof finite type over a locally Noetherian scheme (see\nCohomology of Schemes, Lemma <REF_0008>)\nhence this reduces\nto the case of finite type modules (details omitted).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:29f05720063a68c272f970fbada4ecf139666c372ec4b2e3a1e861b23fae1e35", "unit_id": "tag:05VG:proof"}
